  id: S23_02
  era: "Section 23 \xB7 Economic History under British Rule \xB7 1757 \u2013 1947"
  title: Deindustrialisation
  text: Cheap machine-made British cloth and one-sided tariffs ruined many Indian handicraft industries in the 19th century. Weavers of Dhaka and other centres lost their livelihoods, pushing more people into agriculture.
